{"url":"https://firebase.google.com/docs/projects/billing/firebase-pricing-plans","title":"Firebase pricing plans - Google","description":"For example, you might consider using budget notifications to programmatically disable Cloud Billing on a project. If you use Firebase AI Logic, Firebase App Hosting, Cloud Functions for Firebase, and Firebase Extensions, we strongly recommend that you also set up spend caps, which will pause any new usage of the applicable service if your project reaches the budget set for that service.","extra_snippets":["For example, you might consider using budget notifications to programmatically disable Cloud Billing on a project. If you use Firebase AI Logic, Firebase App Hosting, Cloud Functions for Firebase, and Firebase Extensions, we strongly recommend that you also set up spend caps, which will pause any new usage of the applicable service if your project reaches the budget set for that service.","Last updated 2026-10-01 UTC.","No-cost usage quotas for paid Firebase products (like Cloud Firestore, Cloud Storage, and Hosting)","All Firebase projects are actually Google Cloud projects behind the scenes, which means billing is shared across Firebase and Google Cloud and you can view the same project in both the Firebase console and the Google Cloud console."]}

