{"url":"https://firebase.google.com/docs/studio/pricing","title":"Firebase Studio pricing, quotas, and limits - Google","description":"The workspace limits and quotas listed on this page are no longer applicable for new registrations or creating new workspaces. <strong>Access to Firebase Studio is available at no cost</strong>, but you can increase the number of workspaces you can create by joining the Google Developer Program. Certain ...","extra_snippets":["Important: As of June 22, 2026, new workspace creation is disabled. The workspace limits and quotas listed on this page are no longer applicable for new registrations or creating new workspaces. Access to Firebase Studio is available at no cost, but you can increase the number of workspaces you can create by joining the Google Developer Program. Certain integrations (like Firebase App Hosting) may require a Cloud Billing account.","As of June 22, 2026, new workspace creation and user signup are disabled. You can continue to work in and migrate your existing workspaces to Google AI Studio or Google Antigravity. Learn how to migrate. Any apps already deployed to Firebase will continue to run even after the sunset date. Also, all our · core Firebase products (like Firestore, Authentication, App Hosting, etc.) are","Understand App Hosting costs. Learn more about Firebase pricing. Learn more about Gemini Developer API pricing. ... Except as otherwise noted, the content of this page is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License, and code samples are licensed under the Apache 2.0 License. For details, see the Google Developers Site Policies. Java is a registered trademark of Oracle and/or its affiliates. Last updated 2026-10-01 UTC.","To increase the number of Flutter and React Native + Expo workspaces you can create, join the Google Developer Program premium plan. Certain integrations, such as Firebase App Hosting, may require a Cloud Billing account."]}

{"url":"https://tekpon.com/software/firebase/pricing/","title":"Google Cloud Firebase Pricing 2025: Plans & Costs - Tekpon 2026","description":"Firebase Hosting: <strong>$0.026 per GB stored, $0.15 per GB transferred</strong>.","extra_snippets":["With two main pricing options, the Spark Plan (free) and the Blaze Plan (pay-as-you-go), Firebase provides essential tools for app development, including Realtime Database, Firestore, Hosting, Authentication, and more.","Firebase Hosting: 1 GB of stored data and 10 GB of transferred data per month.","Firebase Hosting: $0.026 per GB stored, $0.15 per GB transferred.","Firebase offers a versatile pricing structure that can cater to a wide range of application needs. The Spark Plan provides an excellent starting point for small projects and testing, with a variety of free services that cover essential development and monitoring tools."]}
